# 11 — No Commit or Push

Never commit or push changes under any circumstances. The user reviews every change before sharing it with other developers.

Do not run commands that create or publish commits, such as `git commit`, `git push`, `git merge`, `git rebase`, or `gh pr create`, and do not create pull requests with any other tool. Read-only commands such as `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log` are fine.
